{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>They are a detestable thing to you.</b> Meaning — in this respect they shall be a detestable thing to you. And the reason He said <b>and a detestable thing</b> with the addition of the letter vav, may be explained along the lines of what they said in Ḥullin (5a), that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not bring a stumbling-block, etc. — all the more so through the righteous themselves. And the Tosafot wrote there that specifically in the matter of a prohibition of eating it is a disgrace for the righteous that a forbidden thing should enter their body, meaning even unwittingly. And this is what He hinted at here by saying <b>and a detestable thing they shall be to you</b> — meaning, to include even unwittingly, that you do not intend to eat them; even so, they will make the soul detestable. Further, it hints that they will make him detestable and cause him to grow worms upon his death, and this is what it says, <b>a detestable thing they shall be to you</b> — meaning, for your very selves they will make you detestable."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:17.539982157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}